# AIDLC Governance

## Directory structure

One directory per epic. Name = Jira epic key or short identifier chosen at workflow start.

```
aidlc-docs/
  <epic-key>/
    state.json           — machine-readable pipeline status + stories (single source of truth)
    vision.md            — vision document (inception)
    adr.md               — consolidated architecture decision records (one file, ADR-001…)
    audit.md             — append-only decision log
    system-prompts/
      context.xml        — compressed inception context
      adr_decisions.xml  — compressed ADR decisions for design agents
```

Never place `aidlc-docs/` content inside application source directories.

## Pipeline state machine

- Each epic's pipeline position lives in `state.json`, governed by `.cursor/skills/state-loader/pipeline-config.json` (valid states, transitions, and skills-per-state).
- `state.json` is the single source of truth for status; `audit.md` is the human ledger. Every status change updates **both**.
- Only move `status` to a value in `transitions[current].next` (or `.rollback`). Never invent a status.
- Pre-design gates: `context-ready` (context.xml) → `inception-completed` (vision.md) → `adr-completed` (adr.md + adr_decisions.xml) → `design-in-progress`.

## Entry point & chaining

- `aidlc-init` is the orchestrator entry point: bootstraps `state.json` (`not-started`) → chains `aidlc-epic-scaffold` → `aidlc-vision-doc` → `aidlc-adr` → `aidlc-design-driven-dev` (HLD → LLD → EARS). It is resumable.
- Every AI-DLC skill MUST invoke `state-loader` first (Step 0) so work resumes correctly across sessions and developers.
- ADR lives only at `{EPIC_DIR}/adr.md` — do not dual-write to `docs/design/` or `docs/architecture/decisions/` as part of the pipeline.

## Audit trail

Every decision, skill execution, and approval is logged in `audit.md` as a table row:

| Timestamp (UTC) | Phase | Skill/Event | Details | Approver |
|-----------------|-------|-------------|---------|----------|
| 2026-07-23T09:00Z | inception | aidlc-vision-doc | vision.md created | pending |

- `pending` → replace with approver name when the user explicitly approves.
- Entries are append-only. Never delete or edit existing rows.

## DOs

- Create `audit.md` whenever a new doc is added to an epic directory.
- Use the epic key consistently as the directory name throughout all phases.
- Render document drafts in chat before writing to disk.
- Archive as `vision-v<n>.md` or `adr-v<n>.md` before overwriting any existing doc.

## DON'Ts

- Do NOT generate application code during the inception or ADR phases.
- Do NOT write any file to disk without explicit user approval.
- Do NOT skip approval gates. Nothing lands on disk until the user says "approved", "looks good", or "finalized".
- Do NOT mix `aidlc-docs/` content with application source code (`iam/`, `devices/`, etc.).
- Do NOT start `aidlc-design-driven-dev` before `adr-completed` and `adr_decisions.xml` exist.
